WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:03.062
(mellow music)

00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:05.529
- [Voiceover] I'm a veteran,
the horse is a veteran

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:08.182
and I can't think of a
better place that he would be

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:09.765
than under my care.

00:00:11.817 --> 00:00:14.074
- [Voiceover] This horse
Quincy is part of an elite

00:00:14.074 --> 00:00:16.184
squad of horses in the military.

00:00:16.184 --> 00:00:19.553
They're called the Caisson
horses of The Old Guard.

00:00:19.553 --> 00:00:22.753
They participate in full honors funerals

00:00:22.753 --> 00:00:25.369
at Arlington National Cemetery.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.100
Over the course of their service,

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.600
each horse walks in thousands of funerals.

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:34.539
When horses retire,
they need a place to go.

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:36.513
So The Old Guard has introduced

00:00:36.513 --> 00:00:39.035
the Caisson Adoption
Project to ensure each horse

00:00:39.035 --> 00:00:41.258
is given to their perfect forever home

00:00:41.258 --> 00:00:43.569
to enjoy their well-earned retirement.

00:00:43.569 --> 00:00:46.057
And that's where George comes in.

00:00:46.057 --> 00:00:48.557
Today he's taking Quincy home.

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:52.858
- We're a very patriotic family.

00:00:52.858 --> 00:00:55.565
The flag flies on the farm everyday

00:00:55.565 --> 00:00:59.612
and it just became a unique
opportunity for another

00:00:59.612 --> 00:01:02.112
veteran to retire on the farm.

00:01:07.413 --> 00:01:09.288
This is a long process,

00:01:09.288 --> 00:01:11.693
they're federal property.

00:01:11.693 --> 00:01:14.291
That's why they spend so much time

00:01:14.291 --> 00:01:17.719
on making a decision to
ensure that these horses

00:01:17.719 --> 00:01:21.136
will be taken care of for their lifespan.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.968
I found out through my
daughter that the horse

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.528
had some health problems
and what they call

00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:30.933
navicular disease, which is
nerve damage on their hoof

00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:35.100
and the farm is a rehab farm
for horses with foot problems

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.292
and many medical problems.

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:40.213
She thought it would be an ideal place for

00:01:40.213 --> 00:01:42.463
the horse to come and live.

00:01:47.253 --> 00:01:49.944
He has his dog tags just like he did

00:01:49.944 --> 00:01:52.824
when he was in the service on his halter.

00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:56.907
Only that the dog tag now
reads “Retired Veteran”.

00:02:02.209 --> 00:02:04.819
Quincy will spend the rest
of his life on the farm

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:09.714
as my companion and, as long
as he has a quality of life,

00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:12.464
he will live on the farm forever.

